{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And it also flows with milk and honey</b> – Because he had commanded them to see whether it was fat or lean, they answered him that it is fat and <b>it also flows with milk and honey</b>. And regarding his question whether it has trees or not, they answered him <b>and this is its fruit</b>, for thus he had commanded them to show him. Now in all this they spoke truth and responded to what they had been commanded, and they should have said that the people dwelling in it are strong and the cities fortified, for they were obligated to speak words of truth to the one who sent them, for thus he had commanded them: \"Is it strong or weak?\" \"In camps or in fortresses?\" But their wickedness was in the word <b>efes</b>, which indicates a thing utterly nullified and withheld from man as impossible in any manner, as in \"Has His kindness ceased forever?\" (Psalms 77:9), \"and there is no other Elohim\" (Isaiah 45:14). So they said to him: the land is fat and also flows with milk and honey and the fruit is good, but it is impossible to come to them, for the people are strong and the cities fortified very greatly, and we also saw the children of the Anak there."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "In the final sentence, the masculine suffix in אליהם (\"to them\") appears to refer to the cities, though it may also be read as referring generally to the land or its inhabitants; translated hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:53.536585366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}